Wings patch 0004: WINGS_FORCE_EMAIL_CONFIRM, no email without a person's click

Upstream's only guard on agent-written mail is the agent_email_confirm setting
(which the agent can change through manage_settings), its staged drafts have
no approval UI, and the agent can bypass it entirely by calling /api/email/send
through its in-process app_api tool. Scheduled-task output, away auto-replies
and plugin tokens send with no human step. With WINGS_FORCE_EMAIL_CONFIRM on
(default in Wings, settable only in .env):

  * _send_smtp_message is a deny-by-default chokepoint: it refuses any message
    not marked human_approved, except automated mail whose every recipient is
    in WINGS_EMAIL_SELF_ADDRESSES.
  * Only a signed-in person's session-cookie request can mark a send approved:
    compose Send, Schedule Send, approving a staged draft, Unsubscribe. The
    agent's loopback calls (internal token header), API tokens and plugin
    routes get HTTP 403.
  * Scheduled rows carry a wings_human_approved flag; the poller sends only
    flagged rows.
  * Adding, editing or testing an email account is people-only, so an agent
    cannot repoint SMTP at another host to harvest the stored password.
  * Away auto-replies are off.
  * In the MCP email server, send_email / reply_to_email create draft documents
    (with a Send button) instead, and SMTP is hard-disabled in that process.

Applies to: odysseus-dev/odysseus@9d0d3720f4ca181d87bef94da826d730acc6d483
License: AGPL-3.0-or-later (same as upstream)

